Navigation note: the web route /period-compare is single-segment, so the first-segment AppRouteParser resolves it
directly via the new route's pathSegment ("period-compare") — no alias needed. A dedicated .periodCompare route
(Insights sidebar group) was added rather than displacing the existing .analytics/.fleetCompare routes (covenant #7).
MenuCommandCatalog.navigateCommands() + SpotlightIndexer derive from AppRoute.allCases, so the new case is auto-covered
(testNavigateCommandsCoverEveryRoute stays green); the pathSegment is unique (testEveryRouteHasUniquePathSegment stays
green); the route resolves to its Insights group (testEveryRouteResolvesToItsGroup stays green). The disambiguation
banner's "Open Fleet comparison" CTA navigates through an injected onNavigate shell hook (selection = .fleetCompare),
mirroring FleetCompareRouteRegistration; the banner dismissal persists in UserDefaults under the web localStorage key
phase40.compareBanner.dismissed.period, and is auto-suppressed for single-vehicle accounts (web vehicleCount < 2).

State mapping (web PageContainer phases + the !a || !b branch): loading + error replace the whole body (web
PageContainer loading/error props -> ProgressView / TSErrorDisplay+Retry); empty + ready BOTH keep the banner +
selectors visible (web renders the selectors above the !a || !b switch) and differ only in the body
(EmptyState vs metric cards + chart + table + insights).

SI note: PeriodStats is stored SI canonical — distance in METERS (web total_distance km x 1000), energy in WATT-HOURS
(web energy_used kWh x 1000), efficiency in Wh/km. Conversion to the user's unit happens only at the SwiftUI render
boundary via Units (P1/S5): distance -> Units.convertDistance; efficiency -> x1.609344 for imperial (web whPerKm);
energy -> /1000 for the fixed-kWh display (web). Cost (currency) and CO₂ (kg) are not unit-preference dimensions.

